  "world": {
   "notes": "MrBeast Burger was launched by Virtual Dining Concepts (Orlando) under a September 2020 endorsement agreement and went live in December 2020, cooked by existing restaurants for delivery and pickup only. It sold more than a million burgers in its first three months and reached about 1,700 locations worldwide by the end of 2022. In 2023 MrBeast sued VDC to end the deal over undercooked, cold and 'inedible' food, saying more than half the locations averaged under two stars and he hadn't received a dime; VDC countersued for more than $100 million. Operators paid VDC 35-40% of sales, which covered brand and delivery relations, leaving about 30% after food and packaging (Nation's Restaurant News); one VDC operator paid DoorDash 30% on its virtual orders and VDC covered the marketing (Food On Demand). DoorDash's merchant plans charge 15%, 25% or 30%. Ghost-kitchen units rent for about $2,500-5,500 a month with hood and utilities. The restaurant, its staff, the suppliers, rent and local events are invented; the licensing fee is an estimate within the reported range, and order volumes are modelled, not reported figures.",
